! TDDFT mode matrix 09/16 -- LR-PCM, EQUILIBRIUM solvation
!
! Same system as case 08 with the response kernel at the STATIC
! permittivity instead of the optical one.  Equilibrium solvation
! must lower the singlets further than nonequilibrium does; if cases
! 08 and 09 ever produce identical numbers, %tddft_pcm is being
! ignored.
%method  B3LYP
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%tddft   3
%tddft_multiplicity singlet
%pcm     cpcm
%solvent water
%tddft_pcm equilibrium
%geom angstrom
O    0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
H    0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
H    0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
